  "language": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "b25",
      "issue": "The clause as amended is clear in selecting New York law, but it is inconsistent with the contract's UK context, particularly clause 5.6 which references the UK Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999. This creates a potential conflict in interpretation, as the contract would be governed by New York law but contains a UK-specific statutory reference."
